WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.520
Vegeta has been coming for Kakarot for decades&nbsp;
now in Dragon Ball – and in the post-credit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.880
scene of the new "Dragon Ball Super" movie,&nbsp;
the unthinkable finally happened. Warning:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.627
spoilers ahead for "Dragon&nbsp;
Ball Super: Super Hero."

00:00:13.627 --> 00:00:16.880
"You need to believe in yourself,&nbsp;
and unleash that power."

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.880
The 21st feature installment in the "Dragon&nbsp;
Ball" series dominated the US box office&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.560
after its first weekend in theaters,&nbsp;
taking the number one position with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:32.080
$20 million opening – twice the take of its&nbsp;
predecessor, "Dragon Ball Super: Broly."

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.640
Of course, "Dragon Ball Super: Super Hero"&nbsp;
hasn't just made an impressive financial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.880
impact. Much like its predecessor, the new&nbsp;
film has received overwhelmingly positive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:46.320
reviews from critics and seems to be doing even&nbsp;
better among casual viewers. The film's story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.560
which revolves around Piccolo and Gohan's&nbsp;
combined efforts to take down a dangerous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:53.920
reformed version of the Red Ribbon&nbsp;
Army, allows "Dragon Ball Super:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.840
Super Hero" the chance to deliver&nbsp;
plenty of memorable scenes as well.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.320
Not only does "Dragon Ball Super: Super Hero"&nbsp;
feature more than its fair share of instantly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:06.400
iconic Piccolo and Gohan moments, but&nbsp;
the film also finds some time to turn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:10.720
its attention to some of the "Dragon Ball"&nbsp;
franchise's other fan-favorite characters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.840
That's especially true in the film's&nbsp;
noteworthy post-credits scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:18.400
which revolves around a twist that some "Dragon&nbsp;
Ball" fans may think has been a long time coming.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.360
Before "Dragon Ball Super:&nbsp;
Super Hero" becomes fully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.880
engrossed in Piccolo and Gohan's&nbsp;
fight against the Red Ribbon Army,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:28.960
it takes a moment to briefly check in with&nbsp;
Vegeta and Goku. At the start of the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:33.360
the two "Dragon Ball" fighters are on Beerus'&nbsp;
planet and in the midst of training. Once that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:38.400
has been established, "Dragon Ball Super: Super&nbsp;
Hero" becomes largely preoccupied with Piccolo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:43.360
Gohan, and the pair's various Red Ribbon Army&nbsp;
combatants. Most of the movie is focused on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:48.000
their fight, giving "Dragon Ball's" less-powerful&nbsp;
players a chance to shine on the silver screen.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.480
However, before "Dragon Ball Super: Super&nbsp;
Hero" cuts to black for the last time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:57.360
the film does take a moment to bring things full&nbsp;
circle and check back in with Goku and Vegeta,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:00.560
who have apparently spent the entire&nbsp;
movie in a fight of their own.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:05.360
At the very end, "Dragon Ball Super: Super&nbsp;
Hero" delivers a genuinely surprising moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:10.000
one that fans of the franchise may have previously&nbsp;
thought they'd never actually get to see onscreen.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.560
When the film's post-credits scene begins,&nbsp;
both Goku and Vegeta are exhausted from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:19.760
their off-screen fight. As their battle winds&nbsp;
down, Vegeta slowly throws one final, weak,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:24.960
tiny punch that proves to be enough to force&nbsp;
Goku to admit defeat, toppling him to the ground.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:29.280
Vegeta obviously takes a moment to truly&nbsp;
cherish his victory, before collapsing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:35.200
the ground himself, exhausted. Finally, after all&nbsp;
these years, he's technically defeated Kakarot.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:40.000
Vegeta's victory over Goku is an undeniably&nbsp;
major "Dragon Ball" moment. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.400
it should be noted that Vegeta gets his&nbsp;
win under very specific circumstances.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:49.440
For starters, his and Goku's fight in the film&nbsp;
isn't a to-the-death battle but a sparring match,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:54.400
with no energy blasts or transformational powers&nbsp;
being used. That means that the two combatants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:59.280
are essentially forced to rely solely on their&nbsp;
martial arts skills and normal stamina levels.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.600
All of which is to say that, while Vegeta's&nbsp;
win will likely still be celebrated by fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:08.240
of the character, "Dragon Ball Super: Super&nbsp;
Hero" does go out of its way to make it clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:12.640
that his fight with Goku isn't exactly&nbsp;
an all-out brawl. Earlier in the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:15.840
Vegeta also takes the time to&nbsp;
meditate before the battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:20.960
noting his belief that doing so will give him an&nbsp;
advantage. The post-credit scene proves him right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:26.144
giving long-time fans of the Saiyan prince the&nbsp;
victory they've always wanted, at long last.

